# QUERY SAFETY

All untrusted values must be parameterized.

Never build SQL by concatenating user input.

Queries must:
- explicitly select columns;
- explicitly join;
- enforce scope;
- use appropriate predicates;
- avoid accidental data expansion.

Before modifying a query, inspect existing callers and expected result shape.
Do not change result columns casually because backend contracts may depend on them.
